# The CORE-ET benchmark corpus: 122 modules.
#
# SCOPE, stated rather than implied. This is a CHOSEN SUBSET, not all of
# CORE-ET. Measured from core-et main `c72b6a2` by collecting every `module`
# declaration under `hw/**/rtl/`: 249 distinct names, of which 31 have more
# than one implementation (the per-technology primitives). The repo's own
# inventory, `core_et_blocks.txt`, splits the same 249 as 215 non-technology
# modules plus 34 technology primitives. So every coverage fraction quoted
# against this file is "of the 122 we attempt", never "of CORE-ET".
#
# The selection rule was never written down, but it reconstructs almost
# exactly. All 122 are real RTL modules, and none is a technology primitive.
# They are the MINION-CORE slice: the name families `core_top`, `intpipe_*`,
# `minion_*`, `vpu_*`, `txfma*`, `trans_*`, `tima*`, `debug_breakpoint` and
# `null_vpu`. 124 modules carry those names; 122 are here. The two that are
# not are `intpipe_mul_div_ctl` and `intpipe_mul_div_dp`, and the omission is
# not technical -- both compile, export and pass the static gates in about a
# second each. Everything outside the slice is the cache and interconnect
# side: `prim_*` (39), `shirecache_*` (30), `rbox_*` (17), `icache_*` (10),
# `neigh_*` (6) and a handful more.
#
# Cross-check: core-et's `dv/rtlcosim/` holds 216 per-module co-simulation
# directories, and 94 of the 122 have one.
#
# DECISION (2026-10-20): 122 stays the declared scope. Adding the two mul_div
# modules would make it a clean family slice at 124; that is a scope change,
# not a correction, so it is recorded here rather than taken.
#
# One list, two consumers: the D4/DCERT2 sweep and scripts/coverage_ledger.py.
# A second copy would be one more thing to drift.
